From aaa3ae145111c848a52199867e89c2df4cf4d609 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Russell Barton <barton5russell@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:15:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] dxdiagn: a missing DirectShow device enumerator leaves
 its section empty instead of failing Initialize

Madeira ships Wine's dxdiagn.dll for 64-bit programs but not devenum.dll.
Far Cry 4's hardware detection (Ubisoft's systemdetection64.dll) creates
the provider and calls IDxDiagProvider::Initialize, which failed:

    err:module:load_dll [dll-missing] ... L"C:\\windows\\system32\\devenum.dll" status=c0000135
    err:ole:com_get_class_object no class object {62be5d10-60eb-11d0-bd3b-00a0c911ce86} could be created
    OutputDebugStringA: "[Gear::SystemDetection::Hardware] ERROR: Can't init the IDxDiagProvider.."

and the game then read a null pointer, as it does with no provider at
all. build_information_tree fills ten sections in turn and gives up on
the first that fails; the DirectShow filters section starts with
CoCreateInstance(CLSID_SystemDeviceEnum), which needs devenum.dll. Every
other section copes with a missing component (display devices fall back
when Direct3D 9 cannot start, sound devices are listed only when there
are some); this one ended the whole tree.

The DirectShow section now behaves like the others: when the device
enumerator cannot be created, or the filter enumeration fails, the
section stays empty (what it found so far is kept), Initialize goes on
to the next section, and one ERR line says so. Nothing else changes.

Device-tested on BCD (a fork of Madeira), Far Cry 4: Initialize
succeeds and the detection reads the display and sound sections.

Signed-off-by: Russell Barton <barton5russell@gmail.com>
---
 dlls/dxdiagn/provider.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/dxdiagn/provider.c b/dlls/dxdiagn/provider.c
index 88011ac..db1eae9 100644
--- a/dlls/dxdiagn/provider.c
+++ b/dlls/dxdiagn/provider.c
@@ -1738,7 +1738,12 @@ static HRESULT build_directshowfilters_tree(IDxDiagContainerImpl_Container *node
     hr = CoCreateInstance(&CLSID_SystemDeviceEnum, NULL, CLSCTX_INPROC_SERVER,
                           &IID_ICreateDevEnum, (void **)&pCreateDevEnum);
     if (FAILED(hr))
-        return hr;
+    {
+        /* Madeira: devenum.dll is not in the 64-bit set; like the other sections, this one stays
+         * empty without its component instead of failing Initialize. */
+        ERR("[dxdiagn] no DirectShow device enumerator (%#lx); the DirectShow filters section stays empty\n", hr);
+        return S_OK;
+    }
 
     hr = ICreateDevEnum_CreateClassEnumerator(pCreateDevEnum, &CLSID_ActiveMovieCategories, &pEmCat, 0);
     if (hr != S_OK)
@@ -1843,6 +1848,11 @@ static HRESULT build_directshowfilters_tree(IDxDiagContainerImpl_Container *node
 cleanup:
     if (pEmCat) IEnumMoniker_Release(pEmCat);
     ICreateDevEnum_Release(pCreateDevEnum);
+    if (FAILED(hr))
+    {
+        ERR("[dxdiagn] DirectShow filter enumeration failed (%#lx); the section keeps what it found\n", hr);
+        return S_OK;
+    }
     return hr;
 }
 
